<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Stewart Parnell</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a>–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Stewart Parnell was an Irish nationalist politician who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-parliamentary-party">Irish Parliamentary Party</a> from 1880. A Protestant landowner, he combined parliamentary obstruction with the agitation of the Land League and persuaded Gladstone to adopt Home Rule in 1886, but his career collapsed in 1890 when his relationship with Katharine O'Shea was exposed in a divorce case.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-stewart-parnell.jpg" alt="Charles Stewart Parnell" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mathew Benjamin Brady / Levin Corbin Handy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Stewart_Parnell_-_Brady-Handy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
